    ACCESSIBLE VALUES FOR THE BAR SERIES (QA FINDING F8)
    ====================================================
    QA finding F8 (LOW, accessibility) measured on the rendered Manager
    View dashboard that EVERY bar of this chart announces "100.0%" to
    assistive technology while its hover tooltip carries the true share.
    Measured verbatim on All Cases by Priority BEFORE this change:

        bar 1 announces "1. Medium, 7, 100.0%"    tooltip "Medium = 7 (43.75%)"
        bar 2 announces "2. High, 4, 100.0%"      tooltip "High = 4 (25%)"
        bar 3 announces "3. Low, 3, 100.0%"       tooltip "Low = 3 (18.75%)"
        bar 4 announces "4. Critical, 2, 100.0%"  tooltip "Critical = 2 (12.5%)"

    ROOT CAUSE, MEASURED IN THE RUNNING PAGE (not inferred)
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    The platform builds every chart with
        accessibility.point.valueDescriptionFormat =
            "{index}. {point.name}, {point.y}, {point.percentage:.1f}%"
    Highcharts computes `point.percentage` per STACK. A non-stacked
    column series puts each point in its own stack, so
    `point.total === point.y` and `point.percentage === 100` for every
    bar. Measured per point on this chart:
        Medium   y=7 percentage=100 total=7
        High     y=4 percentage=100 total=4
        Low      y=3 percentage=100 total=3
        Critical y=2 percentage=100 total=2
    ServiceNow's own tooltip formatter divides by the report total
    instead, which is why the tooltip is right and the announcement is
    wrong. The COUNTS are never wrong, and the donut of the same data
    announces correctly because a pie series shares one stack.

    WHY THE CHART TYPE IS NOT CHANGED
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    The QA report's suggested fix ("render these as donuts") is NOT
    available here: AAP Section 0.4.4 verbatim mandates
        "bar chart for 'All cases by priority'"
    and AAP Section 0.5.1 verbatim mandates "Bar on case.priority" for this file.
    Changing <type> would break a normative requirement in order to fix
    a LOW accessibility defect, so <type>bar</type> is preserved exactly.

    THE IN-SCOPE REMEDY APPLIED: <display_grid>true</display_grid>
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    `display_grid` is a stock, additive `sys_report` column (boolean,
    column label "Display grid") that renders the report's aggregate as
    an HTML data table beneath the chart WITHOUT altering the chart
    type. It has out-of-the-box precedent on this instance (4 of the 182
    `type=bar` reports ship with it enabled), so enabling it is a
    supported report option and not a platform modification, which keeps
    the remedy inside AAP Section 0.3.2's prohibition on global-scope
    changes.

    MEASURED EFFECT, after enabling it and reloading the dashboard with
    the browser cache bypassed:
      - the chart is still a column/bar series (Highcharts
        `series[0].type === "column"`, widget bootstrap
        `repParams.chart_type === "bar"`), so the AAP mandate holds;
      - each bar widget now also renders
        `table.chart_legend.display-grid-table` with a real <thead>,
        `th scope="col"` column headers, `th scope="row"` row headers
        and a bold total row;
      - that table is NOT inside any `aria-hidden="true"` ancestor and
        computes to `display:table; visibility:visible` with non-zero
        offsets, so it IS in the accessibility tree and readable by
        assistive technology;
      - its "Percentage of Count" column carries the CORRECT shares.
        Measured on All Cases by Priority:
        Priority | Case Count | Percentage of Count
        Medium   |      7     |  43.75%
        High     |      4     |  25%
        Low      |      3     |  18.75%
        Critical |      2     |  12.5%
        Total    |     16     | 100%
        (16 cases were present at measurement time: the 13 package rows
        plus three transient QA fixtures that were deleted afterwards.)

    RESIDUE, DISCLOSED AND BOUNDED BY AAP SECTION 0.3.2
    ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
    Enabling `display_grid` gives assistive technology a correct route to
    the values; it does NOT rewrite the per-point description. After the
    change the bars still announce the same "100.0%" strings
    (re-measured on the rendered page: unchanged, byte for byte), and the
    screen-reader information region is unchanged ("Bar chart with
    4 bars." / "The chart has 1 Y axis displaying Case Count.
    Range: 0 to 8." / "End of interactive chart."). Two further measured
    caveats: the grid declares no `role` and no caption, so it is
    announced as an unlabeled table adjacent to the chart; and it sits
    below the chart inside the widget's `overflow:auto` body (client
    height 305px vs scroll height 538px), so a sighted user must scroll
    within the widget to see it and no chart-vs-grid toggle exists.

    Correcting the announcement itself requires changing
    `accessibility.point.valueDescriptionFormat` for column series, which
    lives in the platform's own charting bundle
    (GlideV2ChartingIncludes.jsx / chart_includes.cssx): a GLOBAL
    artifact. AAP Section 0.3.2 verbatim prohibits
        "Global scope changes of any kind"
    and AAP Section 0.7.2 verbatim requires
        "Scope-namespace exclusivity ... zero global-scope writes are
         permitted."
    No scoped `sys_report` column overrides the point-description
    template on this release: `custom_config` (max_length 5000) is used
    only for chart `transforms` in every out-of-the-box row,
    `style_config` is empty on every report on the instance,
    `show_chart_total` is enabled by zero of the 182 bar reports, and the
    widget's Highcharts context menu offers only "Save as PNG" and "Save
    as JPEG" (no "View data table" item). The remaining defect is
    therefore bounded by the AAP Section 0.3.2 exception: it is reported,
    not worked around.

    RE-FILED AS QA ISSUE 11 (MEDIUM): SECOND REMEDY, AND WHAT STAYS OPEN
